From d3a75f8dd6d19a1fbc6b2043c17d3d2a07a028a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mika Laitio <mika.laitio@amd.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 08:05:17 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] propagate HSA runtime through c10 HIP

ROCm executables receive libamdhip64 through c10_hip, but c10_hip does
not propagate libhsa-runtime64. GNU ld uses
--no-copy-dt-needed-entries by default, so it does not traverse
libamdhip64's DT_NEEDED dependency to resolve HSA symbols while linking
an executable.

The original test-specific fix added HSA only to the c10 HIP assertion
executables. That allowed those targets to link, but the nightly build
then failed while linking the bin/hip_complex_test executable and other
consumers of c10_hip with the same missing HSA symbols:

FAILED: [code=1] bin/hip_complex_test
/usr/bin/ld: /home/butler/rockbuilder_ai_workspace/rockbuilder/src_apps/therock/build/dist/rocm/lib/libamdhip64.so.7.15.99004-0000000: undefined reference to `hsa_amd_svm_discard_batch_async@ROCR_1'
/usr/bin/ld: /home/butler/rockbuilder_ai_workspace/rockbuilder/src_apps/therock/build/dist/rocm/lib/libamdhip64.so.7.15.99004-0000000: undefined reference to `hsa_amd_vmem_map@ROCR_1'
collect2: error: ld returned 1 exit status

Add hsa-runtime64 as a PUBLIC dependency of c10_hip. Unlike the
individual c10/hip/test files generated by hipify, c10/hip/CMakeLists.txt
is tracked in the upstream source and can be changed by a base patch
before hipify. Every downstream c10_hip consumer then gets
libhsa-runtime64 on its executable link line.

The hsa-runtime64 CMake target is already provided by the required
package loaded in cmake/public/LoadHIP.cmake.

Signed-off-by: Mika Laitio <mika.laitio@amd.com>
---
 c10/hip/CMakeLists.txt | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/c10/hip/CMakeLists.txt b/c10/hip/CMakeLists.txt
index 0f86f03ca9a..f5c79a0c988 100644
--- a/c10/hip/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/c10/hip/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -45,7 +45,7 @@ if(NOT BUILD_LIBTORCHLESS)
   endif()
 
   # ---[ Dependency of c10_hip
-  target_link_libraries(c10_hip PUBLIC ${C10_LIB} hip::host)
+  target_link_libraries(c10_hip PUBLIC ${C10_LIB} hip::host hsa-runtime64::hsa-runtime64)
 
   target_include_directories(
       c10_hip PUBLIC
-- 
